    "mission_1.compare.arc": "My prediction is the same as the  ideal model. It is different from the simulation result because issues could occur in the robot so it turns less than expected.",
    "mission_1.compare.straight": "The prediction is the same as the result. The odometry result is a bit off because the robot might have other issues that caused it to move less.",
    "mission_1.compare.turn_then_drive": "I estimated that 1.57 radians was 90 degrees which made the final positioning of the x and y to be a bit off. Because I estimated the the radians into degrees I would be off by a bit but it was off even more because the robot could have some other issues that makes it turn less.",
    "mission_1.error.arc": "",
    "mission_1.error.straight": "",
    "mission_1.error.turn_then_drive": "",
    "mission_1.hallway_analysis": "When the robot changes direction when it is near a person. A person might expect the robot to continue to move forward when they are nearby and so the person will move out of the robots way and then if the robot also turns to move they might crash into each other. Can make it so that the robot has some kind of distance when they are moving around people. The trade off is that it will not work properly in very crowded areas. For example have 1 meter between the robot and an object. Can evaluate if the robot is keeping this distance by using LiDAR and testing it in an environment.",
